Add a `network.allowAllInetSockets` policy knob (downstream-only).

Landstrip's `Restricted` network policy mediates AF_INET/AF_INET6 sockets by
socket type and by TCP connect/bind port, on top of the AF_UNIX pathname
allowlist. Agentic workloads here need arbitrary IP sockets (UDP, raw-ish
protocols, and any destination port) while still keeping Unix-socket mediation
and the AF_PACKET/AF_NETLINK denials intact -- upstream has no single switch for
that, so this adds one.

  * config/policy: new `allowAllInetSockets` field threaded into
    `NetworkAccess::Restricted`, plus an `allows_all_inet_sockets()` predicate.
    When set, `restricts_bind_tcp` and `restricts_connect_tcp` report false so
    the port allowlists stop applying.
  * seccomp filter: `build_errno_filter` splits the old single `needs_network`
    flag into `restrict_inet_socket_types` and `restrict_packet_netlink`, so
    AF_PACKET/AF_NETLINK stay denied and the Unix-socket filters stay installed
    even when INET socket-type and TCP Fast Open restrictions are dropped.
  * broker: the connect/bind notification handlers short-circuit to
    `NotificationResult::Continue` for AF_INET/AF_INET6 targets.

Not upstreamable as-is (it is a policy-surface addition, not a bug fix), so it
lives here. See package/overlay/landstrip/overlay.nix.

